  "Question": "\\(\\sqrt8+\\sqrt{18}=\\)",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(\\sqrt{20}\\)",
    "B": "\\(2(\\sqrt2+\\sqrt3)\\)",
    "C": "\\(7\\)",
    "D": "\\(5\\sqrt2\\)",
    "E": "\\(2\\sqrt{13}\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "D",
  "Solution": "Factor out the perfect-square parts so that both terms contain the same remaining square root. Using \\(\\sqrt{ab}=\\sqrt a\\sqrt b\\) for \\(a,b\\ge0\\), we get\n\\[\n\\sqrt8+\\sqrt{18}\n=\\sqrt{4\\cdot2}+\\sqrt{9\\cdot2}\n=2\\sqrt2+3\\sqrt2\n=5\\sqrt2.\n\\]\nThe answer is \\(\\boxed{5\\sqrt2}\\), choice \\(\\text{D}\\).",
